       On  success,  0  is returned, and node and service names, if requested,
       are filled with null‐terminated strings, possibly truncated to fit  the
       specified buffer lengths.  On error, one of the following nonzero error
       codes is returned:

       EEAAII__AAGGAAIINN
              The name could not be resolved at this time.  Try again later.

       EEAAII__BBAADDFFLLAAGGSS
              The _f_l_a_g_s argument has an invalid value.

       EEAAII__FFAAIILL
              A nonrecoverable error occurred.

       EEAAII__FFAAMMIILLYY
              The address family was not recognized, or the address length was
              invalid for the specified family.

       EEAAII__MMEEMMOORRYY
              Out of memory.

       EEAAII__NNOONNAAMMEE
              The   name   does   not  resolve  for  the  supplied  arguments.
              NNII__NNAAMMEERREEQQDD is set and the host’s name  cannot  be  located,  or
              neither hostname nor service name were requested.

       EEAAII__OOVVEERRFFLLOOWW
              The buffer pointed to by _h_o_s_t or _s_e_r_v was too small.

       EEAAII__SSYYSSTTEEMM
              A system error occurred.  The error code can be found in _e_r_r_n_o.

       The  ggaaii__ssttrreerrrroorr(3)  function  translates these error codes to a human
       readable string, suitable for error reporting.

